            <ArticleTitle>Surgical treatment of coronary aneurysm developed after PTCA.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>46-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two patients who developed coronary aneurysm at the site of Percutaneous Transluminal Coronary Angioplasty (PTCA) in proximal LAD accompanied by severe re-stenosis just proximal to the aneurysm are described. Both patients underwent Coronary Arterial Bypass Grafting (CABG) to distal LAD to stop anginal attacks refractory to any anti-anginal drugs and to prevent a rupture of a coronary aneurysm. After the operation the anginal attacks disappeared and no trace of coronary aneurysm was visible in the coronary angiogram.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
